## Part 1: Zoom the in-game camera closer (I pick the zoom)

### Current behaviour
- The world-to-screen scale comes from `computeWorldScale(pxW, pxH, sprites, map)` in `js/game/arena.js`. It aims for a fighter height of `CONFIG.render.fighterScreenRatio` (currently 0.1 of the view height), clamped between `fighterScreenRatioMin` (0.088) and `fighterScreenRatioMax` (0.115). It is also limited by `fitPx`, so the main stage plus `stageFrameMargin` (100) always fits across the view. Then `pixelPerfect` snaps it to whole art pixels.
- `js/game/rendering/camera.js` handles following and framing (STAGE_LEAN, LEAD, FOLLOW_X/Y, floorLine 0.7, clamped to camera bounds).
- `js/game/rendering/hit-fx.js` adds a temporary lethal zoom (`HIT_FX.lethal.zoom` 1.35) on top. Keep it working at the new base zoom.

### Goal
Fighters should look noticeably bigger on screen, closer to the reference screenshot I gave (fighters are about a quarter of the screen height there). It must not be a one-off hack. Put the zoom in `CONFIG.render` as named values so it stays a single tuning point, the same for every fighter and every map.

### How
1. Add a zoom factor (for example `CONFIG.render.cameraZoom`), or raise the fighter-height ratios. Pick whichever fits the existing design best. The "stage must fit across the view" rule (`fitPx`) is what currently stops the camera from coming closer. Relax it in proportion to the zoom: at the closer zoom the camera should follow the fighters rather than always showing the whole stage. Camera bounds clamping must still work, the view must never show outside the camera bounds, and pixel-perfect snapping must still work.
2. Check that the camera still frames both fighters properly at the closer zoom. When they are too far apart to fit, it should keep Player 1 comfortably in view as it does now. Re-tune STAGE_LEAN, LEAD and floorLine only if the closer zoom makes them feel wrong, and tell me if you do.
3. Off-screen fighter markers (arena.js, around the `onScreen` check) must still appear when a fighter leaves the view, which will happen more often now.

### Screenshots for me to choose from (required, do not skip)
Before you settle on a value:
