## Part 3: Refuse screens that are too small

### Why
Playing Alva in a phone browser tab (Safari, Chrome, etc.) makes the game far too small to play well, especially with the bigger controls above. Alva must now refuse to run on really small screens.

### Behaviour
- Decide "too small" from the usable viewport (the CSS-pixel size of the visible area, using `visualViewport` where it exists), not from the user agent. Put the minimum width and height in `js/config.js` as named values. Pick the threshold so that a phone in a normal browser tab (with the address bar and toolbars) is refused, but the same phone running Alva as an installed web app (standalone/fullscreen, see `isRunningAsApp`-style logic in `js/core/web-app-install.js`) can pass if it is big enough. Tablets and desktops always pass. Tell me the numbers you chose and why, and test them against common phone sizes in both modes.
- Check it at startup AND on every resize/orientation change. If the screen becomes too small mid-match, pause the game (online matches: use whatever the existing pause/disconnect handling allows, and do not desync), show the block screen, and remove the block screen when the size is acceptable again. Portrait vs landscape: if the game is only too small because the phone is in portrait, add a line asking the player to rotate the device.
- The block screen is a full-screen, solid black overlay above everything (menus, splash, battle), with centred white text:

  **Title:** "Alva cannot be played on this screen"
  **Body:** "Because we want the best gameplay experience for you, Alva isn't playable on a small screen. Please try downloading Alva as a web app and launching it again to see if Alva accepts the screen size. Otherwise, please try running Alva on a bigger screen, preferably a tablet or a desktop device."

  Put these strings in the localization files (`js/localization/strings`) for every language Alva supports, not hard-coded.
- **Download button:** a clear "Download Alva" button on the block screen that uses the existing install flow (`js/core/web-app-install.js` / `js/ui/install-dialog.js`): on Chromium it triggers the saved `beforeinstallprompt`; on iOS Safari (no prompt) it shows the existing "Add to Home Screen" instructions. If Alva is already installed, or the browser can't install it, the button explains that instead of doing nothing.
- The overlay must work without the rest of the game loading correctly (no dependency on a battle or a menu existing), must be keyboard/controller reachable for the button, and must use the existing visual style (fonts) on a black background.

### Tests
Add tests for the size check (passing sizes, failing sizes, the browser-tab vs installed difference, the portrait message) and for the overlay showing and hiding on resize.

